469| *   its first occurrence in the input array and renders the chronologically
470| *   LATEST entry of the group (latest status, reason, duration, and run
471| *   attribution), with `tryCount` set to the number of REAL tries — grouped
472| *   rows excluding infra-resume (`Resumed`) rows, which are re-parks, not
473| *   attempts — and `resumeCount` set to the number of `Resumed` rows (both
474| *   capped at STAGE_RUN_TRY_COUNT_CAP). Try-count source decision: count the
475| *   observed timeline rows per stage (no schema migration needed;
476| *   `autoIterationCount` is global, not per stage). Rows with no stage label
477| *   are never grouped. Display-only projection: never mutates its input or
478| *   the stored timeline.
