396|/***
397| * MARK: selectDisplayTimeline
398| * @description Prepares stored timeline entries for display in the task
399| *   history UI, newest entry first. Stored entries are chronological
400| *   (oldest first) and must stay that way for persistence, durations, and
401| *   analytics — so this maps legacy numeric stage labels to names, drops
402| *   exact duplicates, then returns a reversed copy. Never mutates its input
403| *   or the stored timeline: stripping happens on the display copies only.
404| *
405| *   Display fail-safe for run attribution: a row headed with a stage that
406| *   positively resolves to a non-agent type (human / ci / merge) has its
407| *   run-attribution fields removed, whatever the stored row carries. Stored
408| *   rows written before the dispatch-time stamping fix can carry a previous
409| *   agent stage's badge on a human / CI arrival row — rendering those fields
410| *   would misattribute a model to a stage that never ran one, so display
411| *   drops them. Rows whose stage does not resolve (renamed stages, empty
412| *   stage list) keep their stored fields: an unknown stage is never assumed
413| *   to be human or CI.
414| * @example selectDisplayTimeline([{ stage: 'Idea' }, { stage: 'Plan' }]) => [{ stage: 'Plan' }, { stage: 'Idea' }]
415| * @example selectDisplayTimeline([], []) => []
416| * @param {Array<Object>} [rawTimeline=[]] - Stored timeline entries, oldest first.
417| * @param {Array<Object>} [stages=[]] - The current workflow stages.
418| * @returns {Array<Object>} Display entries, most recent first.
419| ***/
